1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,460
Hello and welcome. My name's Heather McCallum

2
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:09,870
and I'm one of the potters who work here at Edelman Pottery.

3
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:16,110
Before we go into the workshop, I just want to say a bit about the craft of pottery.

4
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:22,520
Then we'll have a look at the equipment, and you can try making a pot of your own.

5
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:31,281
Like many people, I'm sure you know that pottery as an art form is tens of thousands of years old,

6
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:35,870
and we know this because it stands the test of time.

7
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:43,270
Things like baskets and pictures don't survive in the earth in the same way that pots do.

8
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:47,303
And even if ancient pots are found in small pieces,

9
00:00:47,925 --> 00:00:52,780
they still provide a lot of information about the past

10
00:00:52,780 --> 00:01:02,350
There's no doubt that pottery has given archaeologists a fascinating insight into how ancient humans lived.

11
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:05,400
The shape of an artefact may have been lost

12
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:11,501
but archaeologists can tell whether the pots were for,

13
00:01:11,501 --> 00:01:19,128
say, storage or cooking by examining the impressions on the clay, the scratches from tools;

14
00:01:19,128 --> 00:01:24,720
and the clay itself can reveal where the pots came from.

15
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:29,280
When I ask people why they want to take a pottery class with me

16
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:32,660
they sometimes talk about these things.

17
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:40,948
Like our ancestors, they hope that something they create will also last longer than they do,

18
00:01:40,948 --> 00:01:44,260
that their work - whether it is good or not

19
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:50,790
might say something about humanity many years after their death.

20
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:55,550
Of course, you will all have your own reasons for coming here.

21
00:01:55,550 --> 00:01:57,380
As far as I'm concerned

22
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:04,169
what I love most is the concentration you need to make a good pot.

23
00:02:04,169 --> 00:02:08,910
That focus takes you away from the stresses of everyday life.

24
00:02:08,910 --> 00:02:13,140
If you're elderly, it's also good exercise for hands

25
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:16,419
and wrists and helps with arthritis and,

26
00:02:16,419 --> 00:02:22,260
of course, it's a fun activity for children because it's so messy!

27
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:26,268
Here at Edelman Pottery, we show you some of the basic pottery techniques

28
00:02:26,268 --> 00:02:31,510
so that you can use these to create whatever you wish - a gift for a friend, perhaps.

29
00:02:31,510 --> 00:02:34,332
Like nearly everyone who comes here,

30
00:02:34,332 --> 00:02:40,380
I'm sure this is the first time you will have tried the art

31
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:44,210
so we'll keep things simple today.

32
00:02:44,210 --> 00:02:49,960
Now, before we move on, can I just say a word about what you're wearing.

33
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:54,820
As we said in our email, please remove any watches

34
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:59,370
necklaces, etc. and put them somewhere safe.

35
00:02:59,370 --> 00:03:06,260
If you have long hair, do tie it back now. We'll provide aprons later,

36
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:09,660
but I trust your clothes are old but comfortable

37
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:13,150
not your favourite T-shirt or jeans!

38
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:20,010
So now we're in the workshop. Have a look around - there's a lot going on.

39
00:03:20,010 --> 00:03:25,348
To make pottery that will last, you need a potter's wheel,

40
00:03:25,348 --> 00:03:27,920
a kiln - which is basically a very hot oven

41
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:32,910
where you fire the pottery - and some tools.

42
00:03:32,910 --> 00:03:41,030
So first, the kiln. If you look over in the far corner, you'll see one of ours.

43
00:03:41,030 --> 00:03:44,550
Since their invention, kilns have changed very little,

44
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:51,590
though in the past 20 years, a lot of progress has been made in temperature control.

45
00:03:51,590 --> 00:04:00,343
Basically, a kiln removes the water from clay at temperatures of around a thousand degrees Celsius.

46
00:04:00,343 --> 00:04:06,360
This allows anything you've made to set permanently in shape.

47
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:12,040
It's a pretty ugly, heavy object that's hard to keep in a house or flat

48
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,850
so most people don't have one.

49
00:04:14,850 --> 00:04:20,985
You may think, 'Can't I use my oven?' Well, that's possible

50
00:04:20,985 --> 00:04:24,740
but domestic ovens don't really get hot enough

51
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:29,480
and eventually the clay will crack and fall apart.

52
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:34,040
Some people fire pottery in a fire pit outside

53
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:38,800
but bear in mind that can be dangerous.

54
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:47,820
You also need to know about safety procedures for kilns as they release toxic compounds into the air.

55
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:51,455
Every potter needs a potter's wheel.

56
00:04:51,455 --> 00:05:01,840
This machine is used to shape the clay into an object with circular walls or sides - such as a bowl.

57
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:06,640
Its invention revolutionised the pottery industry

58
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:11,260
allowing multiple items to be produced in a day.

59
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:16,380
Lastly, there are a number of different tools that potters use

60
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:19,280
depending on what they want to make.

61
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:23,520
When you start, your hands can make all kinds of shapes

62
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:27,130
and curves without relying on a sculpting tool.

63
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:34,888
However, there are some basic tools that you will need to handle the clay on the wheel.

64
00:05:34,888 --> 00:05:42,190
Some look very strange and have even odder names that you may find hard to remember.

65
00:05:42,190 --> 00:05:49,412
Rather than go through them all now, I'll just name a few tools as we go along.

66
00:05:49,412 --> 00:05:55,030
We can provide these and I wouldn't recommend spending money on them yet.

67
00:05:55,030 --> 00:06:01,320
So let's try making a pot of your own...
